          "explanation": "<div class=\"ml-en\"><p>$E(X) = 1(0.3) + 2(0.4) + 3(0.3) = 0.3 + 0.8 + 0.9 = 2$. $E(X^2) = 1(0.3) + 4(0.4) + 9(0.3) = 0.3 + 1.6 + 2.7 = 4.6$. $\\operatorname{Var}(X) = E(X^2) - [E(X)]^2 = 4.6 - 4 = 0.6$.</p></div><div class=\"ml-vi\"><p>$E(X) = 1(0.3) + 2(0.4) + 3(0.3) = 2$. $E(X^2) = 1(0.3) + 4(0.4) + 9(0.3) = 4.6$. $\\operatorname{Var}(X) = E(X^2) - [E(X)]^2 = 4.6 - 4 = 0.6$.</p></div>"
