          "explanation": "<div class=\"ml-en\"><p>$\\hat{p}_1 = 10/200 = 0.05$, $\\hat{p}_2 = 8/200 = 0.04$, difference $= 0.01$. Standard error $= \\sqrt{\\frac{0.05(0.95)}{200} + \\frac{0.04(0.96)}{200}} = \\sqrt{0.0002375 + 0.000192} = \\sqrt{0.0004295} = 0.020725$. For a two-sided 99% interval use $z_{0.005} = 2.58$: margin $= 2.58 \\times 0.020725 = 0.0535$. CI $= 0.01 \\pm 0.0535 = (-0.043,\\ 0.063)$.</p></div><div class=\"ml-vi\"><p>$\\hat{p}_1 = 10/200 = 0.05$, $\\hat{p}_2 = 8/200 = 0.04$, hiệu $= 0.01$. Sai số chuẩn $= \\sqrt{\\frac{0.05(0.95)}{200} + \\frac{0.04(0.96)}{200}} = \\sqrt{0.0004295} = 0.020725$. Khoảng hai phía 99% dùng $z_{0.005} = 2.58$: biên sai số $= 2.58 \\times 0.020725 = 0.0535$. Khoảng tin cậy $= 0.01 \\pm 0.0535 = (-0.043,\\ 0.063)$.</p></div>"
